CREATED:20260506T124335Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260506T133347Z
UID:10000099-1780531200-1780703999@go.unca.edu
SUMMARY:brAIn Hub: AI Summit
DESCRIPTION:Join experts and innovators in AI on the campus of UNC Asheville for a dynamic event focused on collaboration\, discovery\, and real-world impact. The brAIn Hub AI Summit brings together professionals\, researchers\, and practitioners to share ideas\, build partnerships\, and explore how AI can enhance both personal and professional work.\n​\nWhether you’re a seasoned AI expert\, a cutting-edge researcher\, or a forward-thinking practitioner\, this summit is designed to provide you with invaluable insights\, practical skills\, and unparalleled networking opportunities. Dive deep into the latest advancements\, explore real-world applications\, and gain a competitive edge in this rapidly evolving field.\n​\nAttend inspiring keynotes\, participate in interactive workshops\, and engage in thought-provoking discussions with leading experts. Discover the tools\, strategies\, and best practices needed to implement AI solutions effectively and ethically\, driving innovation and creating positive impact across industries.\n​\nBreakfast\, lunch\, cocktails and networking events are included in ticket price. \nClick here to register and learn more! \n  \nSchedule:  \nThursday \n8:30 a.m. Registration and Breakfast \n9:30 a.m. – 3:45 p.m. Sessions \n5:00 p.m. Cocktails and Networking event \nFriday \n8:30 a.m. Registration and Breakfast \n9:30 a.m. – 3:15 p.m. Closing ceremony \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \nAccessibility\nUNC Asheville is committed to providing universal access to all of our events. If you have any questions about access or to request reasonable accommodations that will facilitate your full participation in this event\, such as ASL interpreting\, captioned videos\, Braille or electronic text\, please contact Heather L. Lindkvist\, assistant vice chancellor for institutional integrity and access\, hlindkvi@unca.edu or 828.232.5658. \nAdvance notice is necessary to arrange for accessibility needs. All requests must be made ten business days prior to the event. We will attempt to implement late requests but cannot guarantee they will be met. \nVisitor Parking\nAll visitors must adhere to the University’s parking policy. Please visit the UNC Asheville Visitor Parking Permit Registration site to acquire a visitor permit to park on campus. \nEvent Photography and Videography\nPhotography and videography may be captured by University Marketing staff at any public University events. Please review our multimedia statement to learn more.
URL:https://go.unca.edu/event/34157/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://go.unca.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Event-Calendar-TEMPLATE-26.png
END:VEVENT
